{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache, Ascendancy, and The War Within feel like natural next choices because their aggressive riffs and melodic vocals or leads connect with what I enjoy in In Flames and Advance And Vanquish.",
    "The Sickness gives me a clear reason to explore further after Ten Thousand Fists, while Vol. 3 offers the heaviness and melodic passages I want right now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger shares the heaviness of albums I have chosen, but its raw, repetitive approach misses my preference for melodic riffs and developed arrangements.",
    "Live In Texas misses my current interest in exploring studio albums; a connection to heavy rock alone does not make a live recording appealing right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Heaviness seems to count too much on its own, even though the balance between aggression, melody, and arrangement is what makes an album appealing to me.",
    "An association with my rock listening seems to carry across recording formats, although I would currently choose a studio album over a live release."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My strongest choices combine forceful guitar work with memorable melodic passages, rather than simply offering a raw or aggressive sound.",
    "Interest does not always mean I would choose an album now: City of Evil, Mezmerize, and Leviathan appeal, but I would prioritize the closer melodic metal matches this session."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy guitar-driven music, but only some captured the melodic balance and studio exploration I would prioritize now."
}"}
